It looks like this is normal R append behavior.
If vv si the current list of values associated with a key and a new one v is detected then an efficient version of this operation is performed

vv = append(vv, v)

Which is almost exactly what triggered the bug, only that I used a faster implementation. It may have started happening in 1.2 because of changes in serialization but I am not sure, certainly it wasn't deliberate, I will fix the example for now, it seems best to accept that NULL as length 0 and appending things of length 0 creates something with the length equal to the sum of the lengths. Thanks again.

