Antonio,

Thank you for the helpful advice -- as an R veteran who's new to Hadoop, I wasn't thinking of the row-by-row approach that we need to take.  I have been able to get the example problem working with your tip.  One tidbit that took me a little while to figure out and might be helpful to others is that, when using input.format = make.input.format("csv", sep = ","), the first column is automatically processed as the key and the remaining columns are the value.  So this gives the example solution as

res <- mapreduce(c("/temp/test1.csv", "/temp/test2.csv"),
                 input.format = make.input.format("csv", sep = ","),
                 map = function(k, v) {
                   keyval(k, v)
                 },
                 reduce = function(k, df) {
                   fm <- lm(df[[2]] ~ df[[1]])
                   keyval(k, coef(fm))
                 },
                 reduce.on.data.frame = TRUE)

Next steps are to see how this scales up to larger files and more complex problems.  Thanks for your help!  And thanks for the head up about the multirec-io branch.  I'll have a look.

Ian

